#214 is fixed and queued to land, but it isn't finished: the land hadn't reached a verdict when my time ran out. `v2.6.2` isn't tagged and the issue is still open.

**The fix:** `findLatestPatchTag` in `pkg/protosrc/resolve.go` now takes only `vX.Y.PATCH` tags, ranked by number, the way the fleet build already resolves versions.
- A line that has only pre-releases is now an error.
- A pre-release is still used when it is named exactly.
- The new test `TestFindLatestPatchTagSkipsPreReleases` builds a fixture repo with `v1.2.3`, `v1.2.3-rc.1`, `v1.2.4-rc.1`, `v1.2.10-rc.1` and `v1.20.0`. Before the fix, `1.2` resolved to `v1.2.10-rc.1`; now it resolves to `v1.2.3`.
- Commits: `ba249077` (fix and test) and `b413c34c`, which removes the gap from STATE.md and adds a PROPOSALS.md entry for one version resolver shared by protosrc and fleet.

**Gates (local `just gates`):** every gate passed except `current-generation`. All of its fixtures passed, but it was thrown out because I committed the STATE/PROPOSALS edits while it was running. A re-run takes about 2.5 hours, so I didn't do one; the land's own full gate run will decide.

**Land:** queued with the manager since 20:38 UTC, which will finish the merge after this run ends.

**Backports:** PRs are open against every supported release branch: #342 (2.0), #343 (2.1), #344 (2.2), #345 (2.3), #346 (2.4), #347 (2.5) and #348 (2.6). Each one names the next unused patch tag to cut once it merges. Branches 2.0 to 2.5 also needed the `regexp` import added. On each, `go vet` and `go test ./pkg/protosrc/` pass; I didn't run the full gates on them.

**Trace check:** my change touches no handlers. `looper-trace check` fails on main with 9 findings, all already filed as #310 and #311.

**Left for the next run** (in the final checkpoint and in a progress comment on the issue):
1. Read the land verdict.
2. If it landed with the full gates green, tag `v2.6.2` on main at the landed commit (main has had no features since `v2.6.1`) and push it.
3. Post the outcome comment and close #214.
